From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ruiyangke <me@ry.ke>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 00:00:01 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] gpui_windows: Window control, text input and file drops for
 remote windows

Newport shows Linux apps as Windows windows. These apps draw their own title
bars, move and resize themselves and open popups, so the Windows backend gains:

- start_window_move, start_window_resize and show_window_menu for app-drawn
  title bars; set_resizable, set_minimizable, set_maximizable and
  set_maximized at runtime; is_in_live_resize; a native resize constraint the
  Win32 sizing loop applies without entering GPUI.
- Popup mouse passthrough without recreating the window, and a native
  activation handler that runs inside WM_ACTIVATE.
- UTF-16 character delivery (surrogates, dead keys, AltGr) fenced to the
  focused text target, as an opt-in beside the IME path.
- Owned file drops from Explorer, and capture of a genuine left-button press
  for a later outgoing drag.

Every new trait method has a default; other platforms are unchanged.
